Fillets and chamfers: an analytic blend that adds material, whose contact
runs off its face across the face's outline, cut by the faces beyond
growing up to it (mitcad#240).

The case: a boss under a plate, its foot chamfered so wide that the
contact on the plate's underside runs out past the plate's rounded corner
and its sides by a little. The chamfer runs on over the gap and the faces
beyond (the plate's sides) cut it, as 0055 and 0071 do over a hole; but the
chamfer adds material, so the faces beyond grow down to the cut instead of
being cut back, and the edges between them cross the chamfer beyond their
ends, not along them:

- ChFi3d_KPartEdgeCrossing also looks for the crossing on the edge's
  prolongation (a line or a circle) beyond its vertex on the contact's
  face, within the blend's width; the chain of faces beyond is found
  through such crossings (ChFi3d_KPartCutChain).
- The pieces of the chain (ChFi3d_KPartChainPieces) meet at such a
  crossing at a vertex of their own; the edge is prolonged up to it, the
  prolongation bounding the faces on both sides of the edge
  (ChFi3d_ProlongEdgeBeyondVertex), and the edges between the contact's
  face and a face of the chain between two such crossings, all under the
  blend, are cut at their vertices with no side kept (they bound no face
  any more).
- On a closed spine the gap from the last piece round to the first (also
  the only piece's own gap) is filled (ChFi3d_FillKPartGaps); the
  parameters on the contact's closed line and the piece's sections on a
  blend surface closed along the spine are taken across the period's end
  where the gap runs across it, and a cut's p-curve within a relative
  tolerance of a section counts as within the piece.
- A cut that the intersection of the surfaces gives as arcs of one closed
  curve, its ends on different arcs, is taken on that closed curve
  (ChFi3d_KPartCutCurve).
- The other contact of a piece of the chain at a given end, on an edge of
  its face there (the seam of the boss's cylinder), is put on that edge,
  on the seam's side the contact runs into the face from.
- A contact along an edge of its face (0014) takes the side of the blend
  from the other contact's point nearest to it: a piece cut by a face
  beyond has its two lines in different parameters.

Before, these chamfers failed (the walking of a chamfer rolling on an edge
is not implemented). Still open: a closed spine whose gap crosses the seam
of the other contact's face at the spine's start, with that contact inside
its face (not along an edge), gave an unorientable face; 0145 builds it.

